# A parser literal takes the escapes a pattern takes (\n \r \t \0 \\ \'
# \" \xHH); any other is an error, not the escaped character.
# error: literal_bad_escape.grammar:14:12:
# error: unknown escape sequence (the escapes are
@lexer
tokens
    ident
    eof
    err
[ \t\n]+ → skip
[a-z]+ → ident
. → err
@parser
s = IDENT "\q" → 1
